  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trailblazer Sand Lab Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ambition of this assignment is to accelerate the implementation of nature-based coastal protection measures in the coastal area east of Prampram, Ghana. Specifically, this assignment calls for a trailblazer who can coordinate and make connections between different Ghanese and international stakeholders to bring about a supported implementation plan, that can be picked up by the Ghanese government, and financiers such as Invest International and the West Africa Coastal Areas Management Program (WACA) of the World Bank. This assignment will build on the existing Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Ministry of Environment, Science, Technology and Innovation, Hydro and the Water Resources Commission in Ghana, and include international parties in the form of Ecoshape, NL2120, Invest International and Partners for Water. The intended result is to have formulated activities that can be done on short notice, and to have support for a larger project that can be financed at feasibility level.</narrative>
  </description>
